="epo"><addressbook><name>IBIDEN CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IBIDEN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Object: To provide an image processor for a wiring pattern inspecting apparatus so as to make as small a hole mask as possible with high precision for even a non-through hole, ensure the reliability of the inspection of the vicinity of a non-through hole, and suppress false signals due to non-through holes. Constitution: Consecutive pixels of the same type included in a pattern image are counted in each direction from a selected pixel (A) and judged. Since the counting in any direction is started from the same selected pixel (A), pixels do not fail to be extracted and processed even if a predetermined pixel has one pixel width.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention vise à créer un processeur d'image pour un appareil de contrôle de plan de câblage, de manière à produire un masque perforé, qui soit le plus petit possible, avec une grande précision même en cas de trous non traversants. L'invention vise en outre à assurer la fiabilité du contrôle à proximité d'un trou non traversant, et à supprimer les signaux erronés dus à des trous non traversants. A cet effet, des pixels successifs du même type, inclus dans une image de plan de câblage, sont comptés dans chaque direction à partir d'un pixel sélectionné (A) et évalués. Le comptage dans chaque direction étant effectué à partir du même pixel sélectionné (A), les pixels sont extraits et traités même si un pixel prédéterminé présente la largeur d'un pixel.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>